// A forced-above script (fermata, harmonic) on a BEAMED note must clear the beam,
// which floats above the notes — on the notation staff AND the tab, where the beam
// sits a fixed distance above the fret digits. The fermata on the third eighth
// hangs above both beams, not on them.
title "Tab beamed script"
time 4/4
key c major

part m {
  instrument bass
  section A { e,8 f g@fermata a@flageolet e f g a | }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  staff m
  tab m as full
}

// ⚠ THE TAB ASKS FOR `as full` EXPLICITLY (2026-08-29). A tab beside a notation staff
// of the same part now defaults to `as numbers`, which draws no stems, beams, dots,
// tuplet numbers or ties -- and this book is ABOUT one of those, so without the clause
// it would keep passing while testing nothing it claims to.
